QuestGuidance.Register("en",318,{
[10145]="7004A8E1\n1\tSharpen Orkish blades in Cirith Ungol (total: 6)\030Sharpen Orkish axes in Cirith Ungol (total: 6)\tOrkish blades and axes can be found within the Tower of Cirith Ungol. Krúrglok has asked you to sharpen Orkish blades and axes in anticipation of an attack by the Men of Gondor and Rohan.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have sharpened many of the Orkish axes and blades in Cirith Ungol, while also carefully weakening their hilts.\n",
[10146]="70039345\n1\tThe people of Middlemead can be found throughout the settlement in north-western Kingstead. Mágla of Middlemead has asked that you acquaint yourself with the people of Middlemead. You should speak to any villagers or traders you encounter.\t\n2\tTalk to the trade-master, Hildulf\tHildulf can be found near the traders' pavilion in southern Middlemead. You have spoken to the people of Middlemead, and should now speak to the trade-master, Hildulf.\n3\tTalk to Thane Mágla\tThane Mágla can be found in the Mead Hall of Middlemead. You have spoken to several inhabitants of Middlemead, and should now return to Mágla.\n",
[10147]="70042F5E\n1\tCollect undamaged blades in Osgiliath (total: 6)\030Collect armour scraps in Osgiliath (total: 6)\tUndamaged blades and armour scraps might be found throughout the western half of Osgiliath. Meldir has asked you to seek blades and armouring that were left behind when the Morgul-host broke through the western defences of Osgiliath.\n2\tDeliver the arms and armour scraps to Meldir\tMeldir can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath. You have gathered many weapons and armour scraps and should now bring them to Meldir.\n",
[10148]="70000082\n1\tBring the strongboxes to Heikki Goldwatcher\tHeikki Goldwatcher is inside Thorin's Hall, located within the Blue Mountains. Larus Sharpshard has sent you to deliver the two strongboxes you helped reclaim to Heikki Goldwatcher.\n",
[10149]="7004CF31\n1\tTalk to Thranduil\tYou should talk to Thranduil in Felegoth.\n2\tTalk to Thranduil\tYou should talk to Thranduil in Felegoth.\n",
[10150]="7006138E\n1\tDeliver to clothes drop-offs (quantity: see journal)\tGruffo's family lives in homes across Long Cleeve. You should find and deliver the clothes to drop-off spots at their doorsteps.\n2\tTalk to Gruffo\tYou have delivered all the clothes. You should return to Gruffo and let him know. He lives in the house across from the Long Cleeve inn.\n",
[10151]="70041A4E\n1\tCollect bottles of ale for Jajax (total: 8)\030Reclaim Corsair pillage for Jajax (total: 8)\tAle and treasure can be found scattered about Hata Kebir in south-eastern Lebennin. Jajax has asked you to aid him in stealing ale and stolen treasures from the forces in Hata Kebir.\n2\tTalk to Jajax\tJajax can be found at your side, or called with your horn. You have gathered many bottles of ale and reclaimed much of the treasure stolen from the people of Lebennin. You should now speak to Jajax.\n",
[10152]="7000889D\n1\tDefeat Snowreap-trolls (total: 6)\030Defeat Coldeve-trolls (total: 6)\tSnowreap-trolls are likely to be found in the northern stretches of Arador's End, near the Isendeep Mine. You may also find Coldeve stone-trolls, but they have been known to wander the entirety of the Ettenmoors. After speaking to Lieutenant Osur, you were enlisted to assist in destroying the Snowreap and Coldeve-trolls.\n2\tReturn to Lieutenant Osur at the Isendeep Mine\tLieutenant Osur awaits news of your success at the Isendeep Mine. You found and slaughtered the Coldeve and Snowreap-trolls as directed to by Lieutenant Osur. Now you should return to him with the news.\n",
[10153]="7002EFBD\n1\tUrge Thane Utred to evacuate Langhold at once\tThane Utred can be found at the Mead Hall in Langhold. You should return to Thane Utred with the urgent warning of Easterlings and the Nazgûl.\n",
[10154]="70016D08\n1\tUxi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads in Durin's Way. You should return to Uxi, for you have gathered all of the missing pieces of the statue of Helgi Goblinbane.\t\n2\tTalk to Uxi\tUxi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads in Durin's Way. You should return to Uxi, for you have gathered all of the missing pieces of the statue of Helgi Goblinbane.\n3\tPut the statue back together\tThe shattered statue is in the centre of the court, within view of Uxi. Uxi instructed you to take the mortar to the shattered statue and put it back together with the pieces you recovered from all over Moria.\n4\tTalk to Uxi at the Chamber of the Cross-roads\tUxi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads. You should return to Uxi to celebrate the statue's reassembly.\n",
[10155]="7002ED22\n1\tBotulf has asked you to go throughout the city, reassuring the people of Eaworth that the city shall stand and all will be well.\t\n2\tTalk to Botulf at Eaworth\tBotulf stands near the road leading from the Mead Hall of Eaworth to the northern part of the city. You should let Botulf know that you have brought reassuring words to the people of Eaworth.\n",
[10156]="7005480C\n1\tExecute the recipe for a guild-pattern cart\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Build a guild-pattern cart.\n2\tTalk to Viola Brockhouse\030Turn in a guild-pattern cart to Viola Brockhouse\030Talk to the Woodworker's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in a guild-pattern cart to the Woodworker's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[10157]="7005480B\n1\tExecute the recipe for a guild-pattern cutting board\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Make a guild-pattern cutting board.\n2\tTalk to Viola Brockhouse\030Turn in a guild-pattern cutting board to Viola Brockhouse\030Talk to the Woodworker's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in a guild-pattern cutting board to the Woodworker's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[10158]="7005480E\n1\tExecute recipes for guild-pattern spears (total: 6)\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Make six guild-pattern spears.\n2\tTalk to Viola Brockhouse\030Turn in guild-pattern spears (quantity: see journal) to Viola Brockhouse\030Talk to the Woodworker's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in guild-pattern spears (quantity: see journal) to the Woodworker's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[10159]="7005480D\n1\tExecute recipes for guild-pattern chair (total: 3)\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Build three guild-pattern chairs.\n2\tTalk to Viola Brockhouse\030Turn in guild-pattern chairs (total: 3) to Viola Brockhouse\030Talk to the Woodworker's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in guild-pattern chairs (total: 3) to the Woodworker's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[10160]="7006BCEE\n1\tGather wood for repairs (total: 8)\tKûzash has asked you to help him gather wood from trees at the bottom of the cliffs near Ashâgir so that he can work to repair the lift.\n2\tBring the wood back to Kûzash to help repair the lift\tBring the wood for the lift repairs back to Kûzash in the Ashâgir hideout.\n",
[10161]="7002EF51\n1\tFind Dead Orc Glade\tThere is a glade far to the south-east of the Rohirrim camp, in a narrow place between the cliffs and the great lake in East Wall. A great battle between the Uruks and an unknown hero took place there. Wilferth wants you to investigate Dead Orc Glade to learn what happened there.\n2\tTalk to Wilferth\tWilferth is at the Rohirrim-camp in the East Wall. You found a glade full of the bodies of dead Uruks and should report what you saw to Wilferth.\n",
[10162]="70028449\n1\tCollect wart-blooms (total: 5)\030Collect blood-cap mushrooms (total: 3)\030Collect cramp-roots (total: 2)\tThe ingredients can be found throughout western Nan Curunír. You are enticed to collect the ingredients for the sinister recipe and discover what it creates.\n2\tBring the sinister recipe to Ondor in Nan Curunír\tOndor is encamped near the caves of western Nan Curunír. You should bring the sinister recipe to Ondor and ask his opinion of the vile brew.\n",
[10163]="70061276\n1\tInvestigate crates of suspicious goods to collect old recipe scraps (total: 5)\tOld recipe scraps can be found in the ruins. Collect recipe scraps for Wingard Puddifoot.\n2\tDeliver old recipe scraps to Wingard Puddifoot\tWingard Puddifoot can be found just outside the ruins north of Gamwich. Return to Wingard Puddifoot.\n",
[10164]="70000623\n1\tPour the pure water in the Red-maid's sanctum\030Enter the Red-maid's sanctum when the water is calm\tThe Red-maid is in her sanctum within her fortress of Garth Agarwen. Dannasen instructed you to obey Radagast and take the pure water to the Red-maid's sanctum. Once there, he told you that you would have to defeat the Red-maid, and when the waters of her pool go still, to pour the water in.\n2\tBring the phial back to Dannasen\tDannasen is at the Eglan-camp in Agamaur. You should return to Dannasen and tell him that you poured the pure water into the Red-maid's Sanctum.\n",
[10165]="7004AE17\n1\tClaim the first encampment for Gondor\tThe enemy has control of a strategic location in the Mokál Rukh. You should claim this area for Gondor.\n2\tClaim the first encampment for Gondor\tThe enemy has control of a strategic location in the Mokál Rukh. You should claim this area for Gondor.\n3\tClaim the second encampment for Gondor\tThe enemy has control of a strategic location in the Mokál Rukh. You should claim this area for Gondor.\n4\tClaim the third encampment for Gondor\tThe enemy has control of a strategic location in the Mokál Rukh. You should claim this area for Gondor.\n5\tClaim the final encampment for Gondor\tThe enemy has control of a strategic location in the Mokál Rukh. You should claim this area for Gondor.\n6\tCompleted\tClaimed this area for Gondor!\n",
[10166]="7004AE1C\n1\tClaim the first encampment for Gondor\tThe enemy has control of a strategic location in the Agarnaith. You should claim this area for Gondor.\n2\tClaim the first encampment for Gondor\tThe enemy has control of a strategic location in the Agarnaith. You should claim this area for Gondor.\n3\tClaim the second encampment for Gondor\tThe enemy has control of a strategic location in the Agarnaith. You should claim this area for Gondor.\n4\tClaim the third encampment for Gondor\tThe enemy has control of a strategic location in the Agarnaith. You should claim this area for Gondor.\n5\tClaim the final encampment for Gondor\tThe enemy has control of a strategic location in the Agarnaith. You should claim this area for Gondor.\n6\tCompleted\tClaimed this area for Gondor!\n",
